The getpeername fails with EINVAL. According to man page, 
```
[EINVAL]           socket has been shut down.
```

I verified that if we do not close the other half of the socket pair in SystemNative_ForkAndExecProcess, that the getpeer() succeeds. 
However, that makes the tests hang and I did not dig deeper. (yet?)

We may consider something like
```c#
@@ -190,8 +192,15 @@ private unsafe Socket(SafeSocketHandle handle, bool loadPropertiesFromHandle)
                     {
                         // Local and Remote EP may be different sizes for something like UDS.
                         bufferLength = buffer.Length;
-                        if (SocketPal.GetPeerName(handle, buffer, ref bufferLength) != SocketError.Success)
+                        SocketError result = SocketPal.GetPeerName(handle, buffer, ref bufferLength);
+                        if (result != SocketError.Success )
                         {
+                            if (RuntimeInformation.IsOSPlatform(OSPlatform.OSX) && result == SocketError.InvalidArgument)
+                            {
+                                // If socket is not connected, we would get ENOTCONN.
+                                _isConnected = true;
+                            }
+
                             return;
                         }
```

We still won't be able to get RemoteEndPoint if other side disconnected, but all the System.CodeDom tests are passing with that change. Alternatively, we would need to figure out how to avoid or postpone 
https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/feddac7de43999c3f5f9073205d36fd551d746e1/src/libraries/Native/Unix/System.Native/pal_process.c#L440-L442
